{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan-review finding f085c802cc19a0de0 was valid. The CLI guard documentation permits explicit exemptions, but the implementation has no reason-bearing driver exemption map. The plan now states that F12 will add this facility, wire it into completeness checks, reject blank reasons, reject stale names, and reject overlap with offline drivers. Schema registration remains mandatory for every output advertiser. The new acceptance criteria separate exemption metadata from the requirement that CI must not invoke model operations."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787466012165533001,"uuid":"e06aeebf-d37a-4e78-aad7-c355a098e3ca"}